WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.922
Hi! How do we add two four-digit numbers? Today we'll add in columns and learn how to regroup.

2
00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:17.226
First line up the places and start from the ones. 8 plus 5 is 13, so write 3 and carry 1 to the tens.

3
00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:24.546
Tens: 6 plus 7, plus the 1 we carried, is 14. Write 4 and carry 1.

4
00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:31.386
Hundreds: 4 plus 3 plus 1 is 8. Thousands: 2 plus 1 is 3.

5
00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:40.938
So 2468 plus 1375 is 3843.

6
00:00:41.088 --> 00:00:48.162
Now 3507 plus 2896. This one regroups several times.

7
00:00:48.312 --> 00:00:58.650
Ones: 7 plus 6 is 13, write 3, carry 1. Tens: 0 plus 9 plus 1 is 10, write 0, carry 1.

8
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:11.778
Hundreds: 5 plus 8 plus 1 is 14, write 4, carry 1. Thousands: 3 plus 2 plus 1 is 6. The answer is 6403.

9
00:01:11.928 --> 00:01:22.242
Estimate: about 3500 plus 2900 is around 6400, so our answer makes sense.

10
00:01:22.392 --> 00:01:30.954
Watch out! Some pupils get 3733 because they forget to add the carried 1s. That's wrong!

11
00:01:31.104 --> 00:01:38.154
Each time a column makes ten or more, write a small 1 in the next column, and add it when you work that column out.

12
00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:46.746
The correct answer is 3843. Estimate afterwards to see if it makes sense.

13
00:01:46.896 --> 00:01:56.802
Your turn! What is 4250 plus 1630? Pause and think.

14
00:01:56.952 --> 00:02:08.994
No regrouping here: 0 ones, 8 tens, 8 hundreds and 5 thousands. The answer is 5880. Did you get it right?

15
00:02:09.144 --> 00:02:20.850
Another one! What is 6385 plus 2547? Pause and think.

16
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:42.354
Ones: 5 plus 7 is 12, write 2, carry 1. Tens: 8 plus 4 plus 1 is 13, write 3, carry 1. Hundreds: 3 plus 5 plus 1 is 9. Thousands: 8. The answer is 8932. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:42.504 --> 00:02:53.658
Here's another! What is 2706 plus 3194? Pause and think.

18
00:02:53.808 --> 00:03:11.178
Ones: 6 plus 4 is 10. Tens: 0 plus 9 plus 1 is 10. Hundreds: 7 plus 1 plus 1 is 9. Thousands: 5. The answer is 5900. Did you get it right?

19
00:03:11.328 --> 00:03:24.618
Last one! A shop sold 1286 books on Monday and 945 on Tuesday. How many did it sell altogether? Pause and think.

20
00:03:24.768 --> 00:03:36.738
Altogether means add: 1286 plus 945 is 2231 books. Did you get it right?

21
00:03:36.888 --> 00:03:46.002
Remember: in column addition, line up the places, start from the ones, carry 1 whenever a column makes ten, and don't forget to add it.

22
00:03:46.152 --> 00:03:51.642
Next time you go shopping, try adding two prices together!

